irst, the standard matrix of $T$ is given by\n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}].\n$$\n\nRecall that $\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{dim}(\\text{Im}(T))=\\text{rank}(T).$ \n\nSo, we need to find the rank of the matrix $T.$ We reduce $T$ to row echelon form, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T & =[\\begin{aligned}0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{1} & ↔{R}_{2} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ -5 & 1 & 0\\end{aligned}] & {R}_{3} & :={R}_{3}+{R}_{1} \\\\  & ∼[\\begin{aligned}5 & -1 & 0 \\\\ 0 & 2 & 1 \\\\ 0 & 0 & 0\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, since $T$ has $2$ pivot columns, we have that \n\n$$\n\\text{rank}(T)=\\text{rank}(T)=2.\n$$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515655 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "573fcdad-1882-5a89-b59e-937ac9fbdab0" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515655 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186515580 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515659 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515669 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515659 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "64fdc42d-a612-511b-89e1-08887f216d76" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515659 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186421457 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515669 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515671 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515669 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "91c65b99-f75b-572a-b7ef-ec39452cf468" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515669 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186326704 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515671 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515655 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515671 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "9b8c246d-896d-53ae-b740-b5289f2452ef" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515671 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186351273 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515676 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186515659 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515676 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "a46e9e1c-caa9-500c-bcee-929882e141c4" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186515676 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186421455 #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
